            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Both are perforated pipe in gravel that collects groundwater. Weeping tile usually means the pipe laid outside along the footing during construction. A French drain is the broader term and, in basement work, often means the interior perimeter drain installed under the slab edge. Landscapers also use French drain for yard drainage trenches, which adds to the confusion."
          }
