          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I install a basement drainage system myself?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Some parts, yes. Gutters, downspout extensions, regrading, baseboard channel kits and pump replacement are realistic DIY jobs. An interior perimeter drain means sawing and breaking concrete, removing tonnes of debris and re-pouring the slab, which is possible for a determined owner but rarely worth it. Exterior excavation to the footing is contractor work because of trench collapse risk."
          }
